[0.691979, "o", "╔════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\r\n║           Council Discussion: Two-Factor Authentication         ║\r\n╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\r\n\r\n"]
[0.692154, "o", "📋 Council Configuration:\r\n   • Participants: Security Expert, Legal Expert, Technical Expert\r\n   • Turn Strategy: RoundRobin (each participant speaks in order)\r\n   • Max Rounds: 3\r\n   • Termination: MaxRounds (stops after 3 complete rounds)\r\n\r\n🎯 Discussion Topic: \"Should we implement two-factor authentication?\"\r\n\r\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n"]
[0.69233, "o", "📝 Discussion Transcript:\r\n\r\nRound 1 | Speaker: participant_0\r\n         [participant_0]: From a security perspective, two-factor authentication is essential. It significantly reduces the risk of account compromise even if passwords are leaked. I recommend implementing TOTP-based 2FA with backup codes.\r\n\r\n   ┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄\r\n\r\nRound 1 | Speaker: participant_1\r\n         [participant_1]: From a legal standpoint, implementing 2FA helps us comply with GDPR Article 32 regarding appropriate security measures. We should make it optional initially to avoid user friction, but strongly recommended.\r\n\r\n   ┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄\r\n\r\nRound 1 | Speaker: participant_2\r\n"]
[0.692437, "o", "         [participant_2]: I propose using a well-tested library like Google Authenticator compatible TOTP implementation. We can integrate it with our existing authentication system in about 2 sprints.\r\n\r\n   ┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄\r\n\r\nRound 2 | Speaker: participant_0\r\n         [participant_0]: I agree with the legal requirements. We should use industry-standard protocols like RFC 6238 for TOTP. Additionally, we need to ensure the 2FA secret keys are encrypted at rest.\r\n\r\n   ┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄\r\n\r\nRound 2 | Speaker: participant_1\r\n         [participant_1]: We need to ensure proper consent mechanisms for storing 2FA credentials. I'll draft the updated privacy policy and terms of service amendments.\r\n\r\n   ┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄"]
[0.692526, "o", "┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄\r\n\r\nRound 2 | Speaker: participant_2\r\n         [participant_2]: For backup codes, I suggest generating 10 single-use codes per user, stored with bcrypt hashing. We'll need to update our database schema and add new API endpoints.\r\n\r\n   ┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄\r\n\r\nRound 3 | Speaker: participant_0\r\n         [participant_0]: The implementation timeline looks feasible. I'll work on the security audit and penetration testing once the core implementation is complete.\r\n\r\n   ┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄\r\n\r\nRound 3 | Speaker: participant_1\r\n         [participant_1]: Agreed on the phased rollout. We should notify users 30 days in advance before making i"]
[0.69266, "o", "t mandatory for sensitive operations.\r\n\r\n   ┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄\r\n\r\nRound 3 | Speaker: participant_2\r\n         [participant_2]: I'll create a detailed implementation plan with milestones. We should start with a beta rollout to 5% of users for 2 weeks before full deployment.\r\n\r\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n📊 Discussion Summary:\r\n   • Total Rounds Completed: 3\r\n   • Total Messages: 9\r\n   • Termination Reason: MaxRounds\r\n\r\n🎯 Conclusion:\r\n   [participant_2]: I'll create a detailed implementation plan with milestones. We should start with a beta rollout to 5% of users for 2 weeks before full deployment.\r\n\r\n✅ Council discussion completed successfully!\r\n\r\n💡 Key Takeaways:\r\n   • Council pattern enable"]
